# Self-Evolving Chip Design Agent 🧠⚡

A **self-evolving hardware design agent** that uses Qwen3-4B as its reasoning core, surrounded by a memory system, EDA tools (Verilator, Cocotb, Yosys), a reward engine, and a learning loop. The agent iteratively designs, verifies, and optimizes digital hardware — learning from its own trajectories over time.

> **Key Principle**: Qwen3-4B is NOT itself the self-evolving system.
> The complete agent = **Qwen + Memory + Tools + Environment + Evaluator + Reward + Learning Loop**.

## Architecture

```
                        ┌───────────────┐
                        │  User / Task  │
                        └───────┬───────┘
                                │
                        ┌───────▼───────┐
                        │  Agent Loop   │
                        │  (Planner +   │
                        │   Router)     │
                        └───────┬───────┘
                                │
               ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
               │                │                │
        ┌──────▼──────┐  ┌─────▼─────┐  ┌───────▼───────┐
        │  Qwen3-4B   │  │  Memory   │  │  Web Research │
        │  Reasoning  │◄►│  System   │  │  (DuckDuckGo) │
        └──────┬──────┘  └───────────┘  └───────────────┘
               │
      ┌────────┼────────┐
      │        │        │
  ┌───▼──┐ ┌──▼──┐ ┌───▼──┐
  │Veril.│ │Yosys│ │Cocotb│
  └───┬──┘ └──┬──┘ └───┬──┘
      └────────┼────────┘
           ┌───▼───┐
           │Reward │──► Trajectory ──► Learning (SFT/GRPO)
           └───────┘
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
pip install -e .

# 2. Check system status
python main.py status

# 3. Run the agent on a task
python run_agent.py "Design a 4-bit ALU with add, subtract, AND, OR"

# Or use the CLI
python main.py run "Design a parameterized FIFO buffer"
```

## Prerequisites

| Component | Required | Notes |
|-----------|----------|-------|
| Python 3.11+ | ✅ | Core runtime |
| CUDA GPU (8GB+ VRAM) | ✅ | For Qwen3-4B inference |
| Verilator 5+ | Phase 2+ | SystemVerilog simulation |
| Yosys | Phase 4+ | Synthesis & area/timing |
| Cocotb | Phase 3+ | Python-based verification |
| Git | Recommended | Design version control |

## Project Structure

```
self_evolving_chip/
├── agent/           # 🧠 Agent core (Qwen, Planner, Router, Loop)
├── memory/          # 💾 Three-tier memory (Knowledge, Experience, Design)
├── web/             # 🌐 Web research (Search + Retrieval)
├── rtl/             # ⚙️ RTL generation (SystemVerilog + Templates)
├── tools/           # 🔧 EDA wrappers (Verilator, Cocotb, Yosys, Git)
├── evaluator/       # 📊 Evaluation (Functional, Synthesis, Reward)
├── learning/        # 🎓 Training scaffolds (SFT, GRPO)
├── configs/         # ⚙️ Configuration (agent.yaml, prompts.yaml)
├── tests/           # ✅ Test suite
├── designs/         # 📐 Generated designs (git-tracked)
├── trajectories/    # 📝 Episode recordings
└── knowledge_base/  # 📚 Ingested documentation
```

## Development Roadmap

| Phase | Description | Status |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| 1 | Qwen3-4B → Generate SystemVerilog | ✅ Built |
| 2 | + Verilator (compile/sim) | ✅ Built |
| 3 | + Cocotb (functional tests) | ✅ Built |
| 4 | + Yosys (synthesis/area/timing) | ✅ Built |
| 5 | + Memory system (RAG) | ✅ Built |
| 6 | + Web research | ✅ Built |
| 7 | Collect trajectories (1K→100K+) | 🔨 Next |
| 8 | SFT / GRPO / RL training | 📋 Scaffold |
| 9 | Multi-objective optimization | 📋 Planned |
| 10 | FPGA prototype | 📋 Planned |
| 11 | Specialized AI accelerator | 📋 Planned |
| 12 | USB portable AI device | 📋 Planned |

## Running Tests

```bash
# Install dev dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Unit tests (no GPU/tools needed)
pytest tests/test_qwen.py tests/test_evaluator.py tests/test_agent_loop.py -v

# Memory tests (needs disk space for ChromaDB)
pytest tests/test_memory.py -v

# Full test suite (needs EDA tools for integration tests)
pytest tests/ -v
```

## Configuration

Edit `configs/agent.yaml` to customize:
- **LLM**: Model name, backend (transformers/vllm), temperature
- **Memory**: ChromaDB path, embedding model, chunk sizes
- **Tools**: Verilator/Yosys binary paths, WSL2 mode, timeouts
- **Evaluator**: Reward weights, quality thresholds, phase
- **Learning**: SFT/GRPO hyperparameters

